9. PAYMENT PROVIDER AND TECHNICAL HONESTY
==================================================

Payment-provider selection and commercial arrangements have not been finalised.

Do not claim that TOURMS has an active payment-provider integration.

Do not invent:
- Provider account details.
- Payment API capabilities.
- Settlement guarantees.
- Escrow functionality.
- Payment holding arrangements.
- Automatic refunds.
- Automatic split payments.
- Bank verification capabilities.

A split-payment feature is not automatically equivalent to conditional settlement or escrow.

Design provider-neutral interfaces.

Use a payment adapter concept so that a verified provider can be integrated later without redesigning the user experience.

Where conditional holding and release have not been confirmed:
- Clearly mark the feature as a proposed workflow.
- Do not describe the provider as holding funds in escrow.
- Do not show fictional confirmation of funds being secured.
- Do not imply that TOURMS itself is legally authorised to hold customer funds.

Use explicit demonstration or prototype labels where necessary.

